WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.934 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:03.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a legendary Academy Award
and Emmy-winning actress

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
and activist, whose new book
"What Can I Do?

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:09.342
My Path from Climate Despair
to Action," is on sale today

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:13.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
Jane Fonda, everybody.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jane, it is so lovely
to see you again.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.917 size:84% position:42%
-Good to see you, Seth.
I feel for you, man.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:21.154
I can't even imagine what it
must be like playing in --

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we have made
some progress,

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we spoke in April.
I was in an attic then.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so,
while we're not fully back

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
we are taking steps
in the right direction.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you're great.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
I want to ask,

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the things
you talk about in the book

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
is how your activism
has changed.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:39.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, this is something
that you have been,

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:42.242
for lack of a better word,
active in for a long time.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you speak to how
your activism in the '70s

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
versus your activism now
is different?

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, as I say
in the beginning of the book

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the acknowledgment,
you know, when I was young

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:59.692
I thought that activism was a --
was a sprint.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
if I just go fast enough,

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
everything can be fixed
really quick.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:08.968
And then, I got a little older
and I realized that activism

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:09.836 size:88% position:44% line:92%
is more like a marathon,

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I slowed down
and learned to pace myself

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.175 line:92%
But now that I'm seriously old

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
I realize
that it's really a relay.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a relay race.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:24.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
You pass the baton,
and that's kind of what I di

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:28.488
this last fall and winter
with Fire Drill Fridays,

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:30.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is what
this book is about,

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:35.795
is what I did last year and what
I'm doing now virtually.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were a lot of very,
very young people

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:41.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
who were complaining
there weren't enough old peopl

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:44.170 size:84% position:42% line:92%
involved in the actions

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:49.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
to raise awareness of the
urgency of the climate crisis.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I said, "Well,
I'm gonna answer the call.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.180 size:75% position:38%
An aging movie star.
I'll bop in there,

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm gonna
try to make a difference

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.953 size:84% position:42%
and try to alert people
to what's happening."

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:04.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it was the young peopl
that really made the differenc

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:07.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
and woke me
and a lot of other people up

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.730
-It must be rewarding how people
have continued to engage

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.332 size:88% position:44% line:92%
with Fire Drill Fridays.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even it's become
a virtual event.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.138
Has that been something that's
been exciting to you, as well?

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.373 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-It's been unbelievable.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've been doing it now
for six months.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:27.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
And last Friday,
we had 750,000 people

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
following us
across all platforms.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:34.187
July and August,
we had about 3.5 million people.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
And tens of thousands have
signed up and are volunteering

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:42.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
to register voters
and get people to vote,

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.029 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
get out the vote,

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:47.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
Spanish-speaking volunteer
work with the Latinx community

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's just amazing
what's happening.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know you obviously
would rather be doing it

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.173 line:92%
in person than virtually.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess one of the up side
of doing it virtually

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.577 line:92%
is you have not been arreste

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:59.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
for civil disobedience
in a while,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:04.817
because you were really piling
up the arrests in recent months.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:05.852 line:92%
I guess, is it five times

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.720 size:81% position:41%
that you were arrested
at Fire Drill Fridays?

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that right?
-Yes, it is, yeah.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:12.859
-And you were arrested, as well,
in the '70s,

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that was a whole --
a different story

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
compared to what's happene
in sort of recent days.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:21.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Back in the '70s,
Richard Nixon was president,

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was not
a voluntary arrest.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:27.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
I flew from Canada
into Cleveland, Ohio,

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they arrested me
at the border

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:32.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
and took all my vitamin pill
and said they were drugs

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:35.415
and took all my books and papers
and address books.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:37.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the guy --
the arresting officer told m

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:41.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was working from orders
from the White House.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that was --
that was not so cool.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:46.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
This time, you know,
it's different,

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.996 line:92%
engaging in civil disobedience

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not where you start
as an activist,

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:56.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
but for 40 years,
we've been petitioning

00:03:56.135 --> 00:04:02.442
and protesting and marchin
and writing and lobbying,

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
and our voices
haven't been heard.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.813 size:81% position:41%
And, so, the next step
is civil disobedience.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.983 size:84% position:42%
And history has shown
that civil disobedience

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.851 size:88% position:44% line:92%
is what changes history.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:15.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's what we did,
and it got a lot of attention.

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:17.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's
what we were trying to do.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are so many people
in this country

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
who know
there's a climate crisis

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
and know that
it's caused by humans,

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:27.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they want to do somethin
but they don't know what.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:31.537
13 million of them said they
would do civil disobedience,

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:34.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
but nobody's asked.
So, we're asking.

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:38.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's one of the many step
you lay out to people

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.779 line:92%
in the form of solutions.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, obviously,
we are told often

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
what a crisis we're in
with the climate.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:48.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it important for you
in your book to both point out

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:51.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
what is going wrong and also
ways to correct it?

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:54.160 line:92%
Sort of actionable items for -

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
if that's the best way
to describe it.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:57.130 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Absolutely.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.966 size:88% position:44%
I mean, if I was asking,
before I went to D.C.,

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:03.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What can I do?", I knew tha
millions of other people

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
are wanting to know,
"What can I do?"

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:08.975 size:88% position:44%
So, I wanted this book
to be an answer to them.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:12.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
And each chapter, which focuse
on a different aspect

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:16.649 size:88% position:44%
of the climate crisis --
oceans, forests, jobs,

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:19.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
migration, women,
et cetera --

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:23.122
each chapter ends with a section
called "What can I do?",

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it gives people
very tangible things

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:26.993 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that they can do.

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:30.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at the top of the list
is always vote.

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:33.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
Make a plan, vote early, do it
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a good message,
and I hope everybody hears it.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:38.705
I also want to point out
you had a very nice reunio

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
with your co-stars
from the film "Book Club."

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:44.110
You did a virtual book clu
where you and Candice Bergen

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.479 size:81% position:41%
and Mary Steenburgen
talked about the book.

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:50.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that -- Was it enjoyable
to see familiar faces?

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.251 line:92%
-Oh, I love them so much.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's one of the great things
about being an actor.

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:56.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you meet new people
all the time.

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You get to know these peopl

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.793 line:92%
that are so interesting and fun.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
when you're older, though,

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to make a real effort
to stay in touch.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:11.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, last Friday was like
a reunion of Mary and Candy.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.805 line:92%
Diane was on her way to Arizon

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
to buy another adobe house
to change it up.

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's so good at that.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.445
Oh, my God.
That Diane and her adobe houses.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:21.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
When will it stop?
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:25.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know, I know.
But we are --

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.220 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You know, there are over

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:30.423 size:78% position:39%
5 million book clubs
in the United States.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:33.426
Huge number of book clubs,
all women, mostly women.

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:37.630
And, so, what we are sayin
to them is, "If you give m

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.500
a good reason why I should
show up to your book club,

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.603 size:81% position:41%
I'll -- I'll show up."
I mean, it's virtual.

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:46.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'll send you my book,
and I'll sign it,

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:50.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then,
we'll have a discussion.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.679
-Well, that's a lovely offer
And I should note, as well

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:54.881 line:92%
that the proceeds of this book

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:57.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
100% of them,
are going to Green Peace.

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:58.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Correct.
-Thank you for

00:06:58.484 --> 00:06:59.252 line:92%
your generosity with that.

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:01.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always such a pleasur
to see you, Jane.

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:02.588 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Keep up the great work.

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks a lot, Seth.
Good to see you.

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:07.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
Glad you're back on stage.
-Thank you so much.

